From: skrimix <skrimix.git@fastmail.org>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8650: describe the minidump destination word

The boot firmware reads the minidump destination (USB or storage) from
IMEM offset 0x1c, as dload_type@1c in the downstream pineapple.dtsi.
Point the SCM node at it, as Kaanapali does, so qcom_scm.minidump_dest
takes effect.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
@@ -701,6 +701,7 @@
 			qcom,dload-mode = <&tcsr 0x19000>;
 			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
 					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+			sram = <&minidump_config>;
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -7160,6 +7161,10 @@
 
 			ranges = <0 0 0x14680000 0x2c000>;
 
+			minidump_config: minidump-sram@1c {
+				reg = <0x1c 0x4>;
+			};
+
 			ipa_modem_tables: modem-tables@3000 {
 				reg = <0x3000 0x2000>;
 			};
